        "name": "core-must-not-import-the-http-surface",
        "rationale": "``dashboard/`` is the aiohttp + SPA surface. Domain code that imports a handler module inverts the dependency: the domain can no longer be exercised without standing up the web app, which is how a feature ends up reachable ONLY through one route and invisible to the CLI, the MCP surface and the harness. Measured 56 edges across 26 files, most of them entry-point composition (gateway, cli_*) that is legitimately downward-facing. Shrink-only GRANDFATHERS those instead of an exemption list — an allowlist is a thing that rots, a measured floor is not.",
